# Intentfile (A2ML Canonical) — north-star contractile for boj-server-cartridges
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: intend.ncl
# Verb:          intend
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations the project wishes to
#            become. Two sections share one file because they answer
#            the same question at different ranges:
#              [[intents]] — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → done |
#                                    deferred | retired
#              [[wishes]]  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → achieved |
#                                    abandoned
#                            grouped by horizon: near / mid / far.
#            Non-gating — this is a report, not a gate. See the `must`
#            contractile for hard gates.
#
# Rewritten 2026-08-07. The previous version was rsr-template-repo's own
# Intentfile: it described this repository as "the master template for all
# hyperpolymath repositories" and its probes pointed at scripts that do not
# exist here.

[metadata]
project = "boj-server-cartridges"
version = "0.2.0"
last-updated = "2026-08-07"

@abstract:
North-star contractile for boj-server-cartridges. This repository is the
canonical registry of BoJ capability cartridges: the cartridge source tree,
the pinned cartridge-v1 manifest schema mirror, and the validator that
enforces it. Since hyperpolymath/boj-server#300 merged (2026-08-04) it is
the SOLE source — no host carries a bundled fallback tree any more.
@end

## Purpose

Hold every BoJ cartridge in one place, in one taxonomy, behind one schema
gate, so that any host (boj-server, panll, others) can fetch a cartridge on
demand into a flat host-local cache and trust that its manifest is valid.

The three-layer stack is the product, not just the manifest: Idris2 ABI
(proof), Zig FFI (C-ABI implementation), Zig adapter (wire protocols). A
cartridge that validates but does not build is not finished, and this
repository should say so rather than count it as green.

## Anti-Purpose

This repository is NOT:
- A host. It runs nothing and serves nothing.
- The owner of the cartridge spec. That is hyperpolymath/standards;
  schemas/cartridge-v1.json here is a pinned MIRROR, not a source.
- A template repository. It was scaffolded from rsr-template-repo and still
  carries some of that scaffolding, but nothing is meant to copy FROM here
  except cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/, which is the cartridge minting
  template only.
- A general-purpose Zig or Idris2 library. Nothing here is meant to be
  linked against.

## If In Doubt

Ask. Sensitive areas:
- schemas/cartridge-v1.json and schemas/PINNED-SHA — pinned mirror; a change
  here without a matching upstream change in hyperpolymath/standards is
  almost always wrong.
- cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ — every mint inherits it, so a defect
  here propagates 100+ times.
- cartridges/**/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig — vendored by copy; hand-edits create
  drift that nothing currently detects.
- .machine_readable/ and 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml — these are what agents read
  before doing anything else.

## Committed Next-Actions

### adapter-layer-compiles
- description: The 99 cartridge adapters must actually build
- probe: cd cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/adapter && zig build
- status: declared
- notes: BROKEN AND ACKNOWLEDGED. The template adapter calls ffi.gossamer_init, which does not exist, and the ffi `export fn` declarations are not `pub`, so the adapter cannot import them. Every minted adapter inherits the fault. Fix the template first; the 99 copies follow.

### adapter-layer-is-gated
- description: CI must build adapters, not only FFI
- probe: grep -q "adapter" .github/workflows/zig-test.yml
- status: declared
- notes: zig-test.yml filters changed paths on '^cartridges/.*/ffi/' only. The entire adapter layer is invisible to CI, which is why adapter-layer-compiles went unnoticed for so long.

### shim-drift-detected
- description: Vendored cartridge_shim.zig copies must be checked against the template
- probe: test -f tools/sync_cartridge_shim.sh
- status: in_progress
- notes: Proposed in open PR #109 (tools/sync_cartridge_shim.sh with --check, plus a shim-drift CI job). Not on main. Current state on main: 116 copies, 115 byte-identical, 1 divergent (cartridges/domains/gaming/npc-mcp/ffi/cartridge_shim.zig).

### toolchain-pins-agree
- description: One zig version across .tool-versions and every workflow
- probe: test "$(awk '/^zig /{print $2}' .tool-versions)" = "$(grep -oP "version: \K0\.\d+\.\d+" .github/workflows/zig-test.yml | head -1)"
- status: declared
- notes: FAILS TODAY. .tool-versions says 0.15.1; zig-test.yml installs 0.15.2. Open PR #109 moves both to 0.16.0.

### manifest-schema-gate-strict
- description: Every cartridge.json validates strictly against the pinned schema
- probe: cd tools/validate-cartridges && deno task strict
- status: done
- notes: Strict since 2026-06-01. 142 total / 142 passing / 0 failing, re-verified 2026-08-07.

### proof-gate-in-this-repo
- description: Idris2 ABIs type-check here, not only in boj-server
- probe: test -f scripts/typecheck-proofs.sh && test -f .github/workflows/proofs.yml
- status: done
- notes: Closed the hole that let 23 cartridge ABI proofs rot here while their boj-server twins stayed green (#36/#37).

### machine-readable-layer-describes-this-repo
- description: Nothing under .machine_readable/ describes another project
- probe: test "$(awk -F'"' '/^project = /{print $2}' .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml .machine_readable/6a2/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml .machine_readable/contractiles/*.a2ml | sort -u)" = "boj-server-cartridges"
- status: done
- notes: Done 2026-08-07 on branch docs/machine-readable-repair.

## Wishes

### Near Horizon

#### every-abi-dir-has-a-proof
- description: 126 abi/ dirs but only 114 .idr files — 12 abi/ dirs hold no proof at all, and no gate flags an empty abi/
- horizon: near
- status: declared

#### every-cartridge-has-a-readme
- description: 11 of the 142 cartridge directories have no README.adoc
- horizon: near
- status: declared

#### full-tree-build-sweep
- description: A scheduled job that builds every cartridge, not only the ones a PR touched
- horizon: near
- status: in_progress
- notes: Proposed as the `full-sweep` job in open PR #109.

### Mid Horizon

#### shim-not-vendored
- description: Find a way for a fetched cartridge to build standalone without 116 copies of the same file
- horizon: mid
- status: declared
- notes: The copy exists because a host cache is flat and has no sibling paths to reach for. Any fix must not break that.

#### host-side-conformance-test
- description: A test that fetches this registry the way boj-server does and proves the flat cache is usable
- horizon: mid
- status: declared
- notes: Nothing currently exercises the sole-source path from this side.

### Far Horizon

#### adapters-in-affinescript
- description: Retire the 8 TypeScript adapters and 3 ReScript panels once AffineScript MCP/LSP/VSCode bindings ship
- horizon: far
- status: declared
- notes: Blocked on affinescript#446. The carve-out is approved and bounded until then.
